84	  /**
85	   * When warning the user of a lost block in striping mode, we remember the
86	   * dead nodes we've logged. All other striping blocks on these nodes can be
87	   * considered lost too, and we don't want to log a warning for each of them.
88	   * This is to prevent the log from being too verbose. Refer to HDFS-8920.
89	   *
90	   * To minimize the overhead, we only store the datanodeUuid in this set
91	   */
